  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "It is given that \\(x\\) varies directly as \\(y\\) and inversely as the square of \\(z,\\) and that \\(x=10\\) when \\(y=4\\) and \\(z=14.\\) Then, when \\(y=16\\) and \\(z=7,\\) \\(x\\) equals:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(180\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(160\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(154\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(140\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(120\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "b",
    "value": "160"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1959-p20.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Because \\(x=\\frac{ky}{z^2},\\) \\[ \\frac{x_{\\rm new}}{10} =\\frac{16}{4}\\left(\\frac{14}{7}\\right)^2 =4\\cdot4=16. \\] Hence \\(x_{\\rm new}=160.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is B.",
      "hints": [
        "Write \\(x=\\frac{ky}{z^2}\\)",
        "Compare the new and old values by ratios so the constant cancels"
      ],
